From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:43:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 65/69] gdb: do not hide a lost connection while reading a
 library's symbols

A lost connection while reading a library's symbols was a warning; run went on and asserted.

diff --git a/gdb/solib.c b/gdb/solib.c
index 5b2bd96755c..05a180e06e8 100644
--- a/gdb/solib.c
+++ b/gdb/solib.c
@@ -680,6 +680,10 @@ solib_read_symbols (solib &so, symfile_add_flags flags)
     }
   catch (const gdb_exception_error &e)
     {
+      /* Not if the target has gone: the session cannot continue.  */
+      if (e.error == TARGET_CLOSE_ERROR)
+	throw;
+
       exception_fprintf (gdb_stderr, e,
 			 _("Error while reading shared"
 			   " library symbols for %s:\n"),
